# Applies to every `docker build` in this repo (backend and frontend
# images alike, per each's own build context — see docker-compose.yml).
# Mirrors .gitignore's secret/data exclusions, but is enforced separately:
# Docker's build context is not git-aware, so an untracked-but-present
# local file (e.g. a downloaded OAuth client secret sitting in config/)
# would otherwise get copied into an image layer even though git itself
# never tracked it. See DECISIONS.md (issue #52).
#
# Unlike .gitignore, a bare `pattern*.json` here only matches at the
# context ROOT, not at any depth — verified directly (a first pass without
# `**/` prefixes let config/client_secret_*.json leak into a real built
# image). Every pattern below is explicitly `**/`-prefixed because of this.

# --- Secrets -- never let these into an image layer -----------------------
**/config/.env
**/.env
**/*.pem
**/*credentials*.json
**/*token*.json
**/client_secret*.json

# --- Local data stores -----------------------------------------------------
**/data/
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/chroma/
**/.chroma/

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------
**/.venv/
**/.venv-test/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/htmlcov/
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*

# --- Node / frontend -----------------------------------------------------
**/node_modules/
**/build/
**/dist/
**/npm-debug.log*

# --- Editors / OS --------------------------------------------------------
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# --- Docs / VCS / misc -- not needed inside any image ---------------------
# README.md is kept -- pyproject.toml's `readme = "README.md"` is read
# during `uv sync`'s own project-metadata step.
**/.git/
**/.github/
docs/
CLAUDE.md
DECISIONS.md
FLOW.md
